Source of this file: the ONNX export model.onnx from https://huggingface.co/onnx-community/depth-anything-v2-small
(model card licence Apache-2.0).

What was changed: the ONNX graph was simplified for a fixed 518 x 518 input (onnxsim) and converted by
tools/convert_onnx_model.py into one NumPy file; weights of 4096 values or more are stored as 8-bit integers with
one scale per output channel (the depth it predicts differs from the float model's by about 0.3% of its range on
average). It is run by the Studio's own NumPy code (studio/engine/local/onnxnp.py, GPL-3.0); ONNX Runtime is not
used.
